---
import ProjectLayout from "../../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Clim'Act"
  category="Project | Industrial Energy Efficiency"
  year="2024 | 2026"
  description="Collaborative Clim'Act project between Fives entities exploring highly reflective white coatings on industrial buildings to reduce solar heat absorption, cooling demand and associated CO2 emissions."
>

  <p slot="intro">
    A collaborative Fives project exploring the use of highly reflective white
    coatings on industrial buildings to reduce solar heat absorption,
    air-conditioning demand and associated energy consumption.
  </p>


  <!-- PROJECT SNAPSHOT -->

  <section class="portfolio-hero">

    <div class="portfolio-outcome">

      <span class="portfolio-kicker">
        Outcome
      </span>

      <h2>
        What if reducing industrial CO₂ started with the building itself?
      </h2>

      <p>
        Clim'Act investigated the use of highly reflective white coatings on
        industrial roofs and façades as a passive way of limiting solar heat gain.
      </p>

      <p>
        The concept was developed collaboratively with other Fives entities,
        building on previous experience within the Group and studying its potential
        application at the Fives Machining site in Capdenac.
      </p>

      <div class="portfolio-metrics">

        <div>
          <strong>~16,000 m²</strong>
          <span>Potential Capdenac site surface</span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong>2,050 m²</strong>
          <span>Reference roof surface studied</span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong>~20 €/m²</strong>
          <span>Initial coating cost estimate</span>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>


    <figure class="portfolio-main-visual">

      <img
        src="/images/projects/clim-act/clim-act-main.jpg"
        alt="Industrial Fives building with highly reflective white roof coating"
      />

      <figcaption>
        Clim'Act | Passive reduction of solar heat gain through reflective surfaces
      </figcaption>

    </figure>

  </section>


  <!-- 01 | CONTEXT -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      01
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Context
      </h2>

      <p>
        Clim'Act is a Fives Group initiative encouraging employees and business
        units to propose practical solutions for reducing environmental impact.
      </p>

      <p>
        My proposal was selected and developed in collaboration with Fives Cryo,
        with contributions from other parts of the Group.
      </p>

      <p>
        The project focused on a simple question:
        could the external colour and solar reflectivity of industrial buildings
        measurably reduce their cooling requirements?
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 02 | PHYSICAL PRINCIPLE -->

  <section class="portfolio-visual-section">

    <div class="portfolio-section-header">

      <span>
        02 | Physical principle
      </span>

      <h2>
        Reflect more. Absorb less.
      </h2>

    </div>


    <div class="process-grid">

      <figure>

        <img
          src="/images/projects/clim-act/dark-roof.jpg"
          alt="Solar radiation absorbed by a dark industrial roof"
        />

        <figcaption>
          01 | Conventional surface | Higher solar absorption
        </figcaption>

      </figure>


      <figure>

        <img
          src="/images/projects/clim-act/white-roof.jpg"
          alt="Solar radiation reflected by a white industrial roof"
        />

        <figcaption>
          02 | Reflective surface | Higher solar reflection
        </figcaption>

      </figure>


      <figure>

        <img
          src="/images/projects/clim-act/thermal-comparison.jpg"
          alt="Thermal comparison between conventional and reflective roofs"
        />

        <figcaption>
          03 | Reduced thermal load on the building
        </figcaption>

      </figure>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 03 | ENGINEERING IDEA -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      03
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Engineering idea
      </h2>

      <p>
        Dark roofing and façade materials absorb a significant portion of incoming
        solar radiation and convert it into heat.
      </p>

      <p>
        By replacing or covering these surfaces with a highly reflective white
        coating, a larger proportion of solar energy can be reflected before it
        enters the building envelope.
      </p>

      <p>
        This passive measure can reduce internal heat gains and therefore reduce
        the workload required from air-conditioning systems during warm periods.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 04 | MY CONTRIBUTION -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      04
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        My contribution
      </h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Proposed the reflective building concept within Clim'Act
        </li>

        <li>
          Studied the physical principles behind solar reflectivity
        </li>

        <li>
          Researched reflective coating solutions
        </li>

        <li>
          Evaluated potential application to Fives industrial buildings
        </li>

        <li>
          Developed preliminary economic estimates
        </li>

        <li>
          Worked with Fives Cryo on the project
        </li>

        <li>
          Prepared technical material to support the proposal
        </li>

      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 05 | SITE STUDY -->

  <section class="portfolio-system">

    <div class="portfolio-section-header">

      <span>
        05 | Site study
      </span>

      <h2>
        From concept to industrial scale.
      </h2>

    </div>


    <div class="system-grid">

      <figure class="system-overview">

        <img
          src="/images/projects/clim-act/site-overview.jpg"
          alt="Fives Machining Capdenac industrial site"
        />

        <figcaption>
          Site-level study | Potential application at Fives Machining Capdenac
        </figcaption>

      </figure>


      <div class="subsystem-stack">

        <figure>

          <img
            src="/images/projects/clim-act/roof-area.jpg"
            alt="Industrial roof surface considered for reflective coating"
          />

          <figcaption>
            Roof surfaces | Main solar-exposed areas
          </figcaption>

        </figure>


        <div class="subsystem-copy">

          <h3>
            Scaling the concept
          </h3>

          <p>
            A first costing exercise was based on approximately 2,050 m² of
            painted metal roofing.
          </p>

          <p>
            The wider Capdenac site represented a much larger potential surface,
            allowing the project to explore how industrial-scale deployment could
            affect both investment and unit cost.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 06 | ECONOMIC STUDY -->

  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      06
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Economic study
      </h2>

      <p>
        Preliminary estimates for a reference surface of approximately
        2,050 m² placed the coating operation in the range of
        €40,000 to €50,000.
      </p>

      <p>
        This corresponded to an initial order of magnitude of approximately
        €20 per square metre.
      </p>

      <p>
        A dedicated Cool Roof assessment was also considered, with an estimated
        study cost of around €2,500.
      </p>

      <p>
        Because the total Capdenac surface considered could reach approximately
        16,000 m², larger-scale deployment also offered the possibility of
        improved commercial conditions.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- 07 | IMPACT CHAIN -->

  <section class="portfolio-wide-visual">

    <figure>

      <img
        src="/images/projects/clim-act/impact-chain.jpg"
        alt="Relationship between reflective coating, solar heat gain, cooling demand and CO2 emissions"
      />

      <figcaption>
        Impact chain | Solar reflection → lower heat gain → lower cooling demand → lower electricity consumption
      </figcaption>

    </figure>

  </section>


